Nautilus.Integrate.gauss_legendre_5: n_points must be 5

The ordering pin for the guard, in the uniform case. `gl5_require_n_points`
is a checked pass-through on `half_range`, the block's first binding, so
strict evaluation reaches the check before `f` is applied at any node. The
integrand here traps if it is ever called, so this file would report the
integrand's message instead if the guard ran late or was dropped.

Two companions make this non-vacuous rather than asserting it in prose.
`gauss_legendre_5_integrand_reachable_neg` is this same integrand at
`n_points = 5`, and does report the integrand's message, so the integrand is
reachable. `gauss_legendre_5_midpoint_node_neg` covers the one node that
`half_range` does not reach.
